# This tree is cloned on Windows and on Linux, and with no rules here each clone
# decides line endings for itself from its own core.autocrlf -- which is where
# the drift comes from. Every text file in this repository is LF and always has
# been; these rules make that a property of the repository rather than of
# whoever happened to clone it, and of how.
#
# UCC compiles LF sources perfectly well, so this costs the build nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Said outright rather than left to git's text/binary heuristic, which decides
# on NUL bytes alone: some UnrealScript sources carry raw control bytes inside
# string literals (colour codes), and that is a poor thing to have guessed
# wrong about.
*.uc  text eol=lf
*.uci text eol=lf

# Content rather than source -- git should not look inside it or rewrite a byte
# of it. Upper-case variants are listed because these patterns are
# case-sensitive and both spellings are in the tree.
*.dds binary
*.lwo binary
*.png binary
*.tga binary
*.TGA binary
*.usx binary
*.utx binary
*.wav binary
*.WAV binary
